/// getting close to your account-level quotas. The per-table quotas apply
/// only when you are creating a new table. They restrict the sum of the
/// provisioned capacity of the new table itself and all its global
/// secondary indexes. For existing tables and their GSIs, DynamoDB doesn't
/// let you increase provisioned capacity extremely rapidly, but the only
/// quota that applies is that the aggregate provisioned capacity over all
/// your tables and GSIs cannot exceed either of the per-account quotas.
